%T A402367 5159730,5703337,5905148,5966889,5981086,5983145,5983272,6976946,
%U A402367 7178757,7240498,7254695,7256754,7256881,7722364,7784105,7798302,7800361,7800488,7985916,8000113,8002172,8002299,8061854
%N A402367 Numbers that are the sum of seven distinct positive 7th powers.
%e A402367 a(1) = Sum_{k=1..7} k^7 = A031971(7) is clearly the smallest such number.
%e A402367 a(2) = Sum_{k=1..6} k^7 + 8^7 is the next larger such number, then
%e A402367 a(3) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^7 - 6^7 (i.e., 6^7 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402367 a(4) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^7 - 5^7 (i.e., 6^7 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402367 a(5) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^7 - 4^7 (i.e., 6^7 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402367 a(6) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^7 - 3^7 (i.e., 6^7 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402367 a(7) = Sum_{k=1..8} k^7 - 2^7 (i.e., 6^7 is omitted in the sum)
%e A402367 a(8) = Sum_{k=2..8} k^7.
%e A402367 We see that the first 8 terms are a(n) = a(8)+1 - (9-n)^7, 1 <= n <= 7.
%e A402367 Then the sequence goes on with 2 omitted terms among {k^7, 1 <= k <= 9}, then with 3 omitted terms among {k^7, 1 <= k <= 10}, etc. This pattern breaks when m^7 < Sum_{k=m-7..m-1} k^7, which happens for m = 12. Then there will be sums with largest term 12^7 that are smaller than some sums with largest term 11^7.
%o A402367 (PARI) A402367_first(n=50, k=7)=my(L=List(),m=k); while(#L<n^1.05, forvec(v=vector(k,i,[m^(i==k),m]), listput(L,sum(i=1,k,v[i]^k)), 2); m++); Set(L)[1..n]
%Y A402367 Cf. A001015 (seventh powers), A031971 (Sum k^n, k=1..n).
%Y A402367 Row 7 of A402364 (n-th row lists sums of n distinct n-th powers > 0).
%Y A402367 Cf. A004431 (sums of two distinct squares > 0), A024975 (sums of 3 distinct cubes > 0), A176197 (sums of 4 distinct 4th powers > 0), A402365 (sums of 5 distinct 5th powers > 0), A402366 (sums of 6 distinct 6th powers > 0), A402368 (sums of 8 distinct 8th powers > 0), ...
%K A402367 nonn,new
